  "caveats": [
    "The offset model is fitted on the training papers' shrunk residuals and applied to the held-out papers' metadata. Because a DOI fold holds out whole papers, a test paper contributes no rows to the offset fit -- but its metadata (which metals, which cells, which scaffolds) is used, and that is only legitimate if the compound set is known before the assay is read.",
    "n_rows and n_ligands are excluded from the primary set because the frozen no-leak rule forbids test-fold row counts. The design+counts arm shows what they would add.",
    "The design+outcome arm uses the test paper's own y mean and deciles. It is a leaky upper bound and is labelled as such; it is not a result.",
    "LOPO ridge R2 is computed on the first outer fold only, to keep the runtime bounded; it describes the offset model, not the final prediction.",
    "Offsets are shrunk by n/(n+10); a two-row paper cannot move its own prediction by a log unit, which also caps how much a small test paper can be corrected."
  ]
}
